Hey, Phong.

291
00:28:03,960 --> 00:28:04,480
Hmm?

292
00:28:04,880 --> 00:28:05,840
What about Inspector Ken?

293
00:28:08,800 --> 00:28:09,600
Let's go to work first.

294
00:28:10,400 --> 00:28:10,800
Right?

295
00:28:11,440 --> 00:28:12,520
You've been off for several days.

296
00:28:12,640 --> 00:28:13,840
You have a lot to catch up on.

297
00:28:13,840 --> 00:28:14,560
Come here.

298
00:28:15,360 --> 00:28:15,960
Come here.

299
00:30:26,360 --> 00:30:26,960
Look.

300
00:30:28,560 --> 00:30:29,200
Look at this.

301
00:30:30,320 --> 00:30:31,760
My wound hasn't even healed yet.

302
00:31:25,120 --> 00:31:25,880
From now on,

303
00:31:27,360 --> 00:31:28,400
I'll teach you

304
00:31:29,440 --> 00:31:31,160
how to live like a normal human.

305
00:32:06,640 --> 00:32:07,080
Hey.

306
00:32:07,440 --> 00:32:08,000
Inspector.

307
00:32:08,840 --> 00:32:09,360
Inspector.

308
00:32:10,920 --> 00:32:11,480
Hello.

309
00:32:12,520 --> 00:32:13,200
What are you doing here?

310
00:32:13,760 --> 00:32:14,720
I was just passing by.

311
00:32:15,560 --> 00:32:16,080
Oh.

312
00:32:17,840 --> 00:32:19,160
How have you been?

313
00:32:20,120 --> 00:32:20,960
Much better.

314
00:32:21,880 --> 00:32:23,080
When I went home and saw my mother,

315
00:32:23,200 --> 00:32:24,680
she seemed to be
coping better than I expected.

316
00:32:25,520 --> 00:32:26,480
I think I can do the same.

317
00:32:29,360 --> 00:32:31,280
Nin has me as his friend.

318
00:32:31,680 --> 00:32:33,200
I won't let him stay sad.

319
00:32:33,440 --> 00:32:34,280
Don't worry.

320
00:32:36,800 --> 00:32:37,880
I'm jealous of you guys

321
00:32:38,280 --> 00:32:39,160
for still having each other.

322
00:32:42,280 --> 00:32:42,720
Yeah.

323
00:32:44,080 --> 00:32:45,240
There are so many things

324
00:32:45,960 --> 00:32:47,320
I want to tell someone.

325
00:32:48,960 --> 00:32:49,720
But

326
00:32:51,400 --> 00:32:52,600
he's no longer here for me to tell him.

327
00:32:56,640 --> 00:32:57,160
Thank you.

328
00:32:58,400 --> 00:32:59,960
If you have something
to tell someone, tell them now.

329
00:33:00,600 --> 00:33:01,280
Life is short.

330
00:33:01,960 --> 00:33:02,560
I'm going.

331
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:04,120
Okay.

332
00:33:06,560 --> 00:33:07,120
See you.

333
00:33:13,800 --> 00:33:14,280
Nin.

334
00:33:17,680 --> 00:33:18,880
I...

335
00:33:19,360 --> 00:33:20,600
have something I want to tell you.

336
00:33:21,360 --> 00:33:22,000
Right here?

337
00:33:25,160 --> 00:33:25,640
Well...

338
00:33:27,520 --> 00:33:28,760
Thank you

339
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:30,280
for taking pictures of me.

340
00:33:31,400 --> 00:33:34,400
You know you're the only one
who can make me look good in photos.

341
00:33:36,240 --> 00:33:39,440
And you're the only one
who knows my best angles.

342
00:33:41,920 --> 00:33:42,600
Normally,

343
00:33:42,640 --> 00:33:43,680
we don't really hug.

344
00:33:44,160 --> 00:33:45,240
Can I hug you?

345
00:33:55,600 --> 00:33:56,200
You know,

346
00:33:58,280 --> 00:34:00,840
you're the only person I feel safe with.

347
00:34:02,320 --> 00:34:03,520
I don't have to care about anyone else,

348
00:34:05,920 --> 00:34:07,240
and I don't have to worry

349
00:34:07,400 --> 00:34:08,520
about what they think of me.

350
00:34:09,760 --> 00:34:10,360
Because

351
00:34:11,440 --> 00:34:12,720
no matter what I do,

352
00:34:13,280 --> 00:34:14,640
you'll always be there for me,

353
00:34:15,640 --> 00:34:16,800
and you'll never leave.

354
00:34:21,560 --> 00:34:22,240
But today,

355
00:34:23,400 --> 00:34:25,080
I'm afraid

356
00:34:26,400 --> 00:34:28,400
that if I tell you, you might leave.

357
00:34:32,360 --> 00:34:33,280
But I've made up my mind.

358
00:34:34,440 --> 00:34:34,920
I'm going to tell you.

359
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:40,720
And what I want to say is...

360
00:34:41,880 --> 00:34:42,560
- I like...
- I like you.

361
00:34:44,520 --> 00:34:44,920
Huh?

362
00:34:47,120 --> 00:34:48,160
I like you too.

363
00:34:49,520 --> 00:34:50,920
The same way you've always liked me.

364
00:34:59,480 --> 00:35:00,880
I know how you feel about me.

365
00:35:02,040 --> 00:35:03,080
I feel the same way.

366
00:35:04,920 --> 00:35:05,960
But I love you too much,

367
00:35:08,240 --> 00:35:09,520
so I've always pretended not to know.

368
00:35:12,120 --> 00:35:13,360
I don't want us to break up someday.

369
00:35:14,400 --> 00:35:16,240
To break up, end things,
and go our separate ways.

370
00:35:17,640 --> 00:35:18,600
I think if that's how it'll end,

371
00:35:19,480 --> 00:35:20,880
we'd be better off as friends.

372
00:35:22,040 --> 00:35:22,920
Because if we're friends,

373
00:35:24,120 --> 00:35:25,240
I can keep you in my life.

374
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:29,240
But friends don't kiss.

375
00:35:31,440 --> 00:35:32,800
If you really wanted to be my friend,

376
00:35:33,520 --> 00:35:34,840
you wouldn't have kissed me that day.

377
00:35:36,040 --> 00:35:36,840
And besides,

378
00:35:37,760 --> 00:35:39,040
who starts dating just to break up?

379
00:35:40,240 --> 00:35:41,320
I...

380
00:35:41,920 --> 00:35:42,560
How about this?

381
00:35:43,440 --> 00:35:44,320
Make a bet with me.

382
00:35:45,800 --> 00:35:47,440
I'll stay by your side forever,

383
00:35:47,440 --> 00:35:48,480
no matter what happens.

384
00:35:52,560 --> 00:35:53,280
But let me ask you something.

385
00:35:55,600 --> 00:35:57,680
Can I stay by your side
as your boyfriend?

386
00:36:05,440 --> 00:36:06,400
Can I kiss you?

387
00:36:08,600 --> 00:36:09,400
Right here?

388
00:36:12,280 --> 00:36:15,680
♪How deep the scars
that life had carved♪

389
00:36:15,680 --> 00:36:19,160
♪How long the nights
where courage starved♪

390
00:36:19,160 --> 00:36:22,560
♪I walked this path,
through dust, through all♪

391
00:36:22,560 --> 00:36:25,880
♪Carried on, though strength would fall♪

392
00:36:25,880 --> 00:36:29,280
♪I viewed life plain without dismay♪

393
00:36:29,280 --> 00:36:31,400
♪Cruel tales bring grief
that won't decay♪

394
00:36:31,400 --> 00:36:32,240
I'm embarrassed.

395
00:36:33,080 --> 00:36:33,440
Don't.

396
00:36:34,040 --> 00:36:34,840
Hey, no.

397
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:36,960
There are people around.
Someone might see us.

398
00:36:37,200 --> 00:36:37,960
That's enough.

399
00:36:40,680 --> 00:36:41,040
Let's go.

400
00:36:43,160 --> 00:36:44,480
You're buying me dinner today.

401
00:36:45,480 --> 00:36:46,040
Fine.

402
00:36:55,440 --> 00:36:57,840
- Let's have a toast.
- Cheers.

403
00:36:58,080 --> 00:36:59,080
Just a sip.

404
00:37:02,720 --> 00:37:03,960
How's your wound?

405
00:37:04,880 --> 00:37:06,040
You're barely healed
and already drinking.

406
00:37:07,960 --> 00:37:09,760
Just drink. Why be sad?

407
00:37:10,520 --> 00:37:10,920
Drink.

408
00:37:11,680 --> 00:37:12,640
Don't think too much.

409
00:37:13,200 --> 00:37:14,320
This is normal.

410
00:37:15,120 --> 00:37:16,760
Let's just enjoy ourselves.

411
00:37:17,440 --> 00:37:18,480
It's a blessing you survived.

412
00:37:18,800 --> 00:37:20,640
Your wound was huge that day.

413
00:37:22,160 --> 00:37:24,120
You're lucky you made it.

414
00:37:24,120 --> 00:37:24,720
You okay?

415
00:37:25,400 --> 00:37:26,320
Just a little.

416
00:37:26,320 --> 00:37:27,720
Let's toast first. We might not
get another chance.

417
00:37:28,560 --> 00:37:29,600
Come on.

418
00:37:33,240 --> 00:37:34,160
He's being transferred.

419
00:37:37,520 --> 00:37:38,640
Will you come back to visit?

420
00:37:48,480 --> 00:37:49,000
James.

421
00:37:49,720 --> 00:37:50,680
Let me ask you something.

422
00:37:51,760 --> 00:37:53,440
You decided to go back to Bangkok

423
00:37:54,120 --> 00:37:55,800
partly because of Inspector Ken, right?

424
00:37:59,440 --> 00:38:01,840
Actually, the higher-ups want this
whole thing to end quietly.

425
00:38:03,480 --> 00:38:05,120
So they told everyone
not to talk about it.

426
00:38:06,400 --> 00:38:08,880
But I see you as my little brother.

427
00:38:09,440 --> 00:38:10,240
What is it, Phong?

428
00:38:10,240 --> 00:38:11,600
So I'm going to tell you.

429
00:38:18,520 --> 00:38:19,080
Oh...

430
00:38:59,320 --> 00:38:59,960
Right now,

431
00:39:01,760 --> 00:39:03,960
there's only one person I love left.

432
00:39:06,440 --> 00:39:07,120
And that's you.

433
00:39:09,000 --> 00:39:09,920
You...

434
00:39:11,920 --> 00:39:15,200
Are you really going to get back
at me by killing yourself?

435
00:40:37,200 --> 00:40:39,160
I'll make sure
you see it with your own eyes.

436
00:40:40,920 --> 00:40:43,600
I'll drive you somewhere
you can see a rainbow up close.

437
00:40:44,600 --> 00:40:46,560
Close enough to see all seven colors.

438
00:40:47,440 --> 00:40:48,400
I promise.

439
00:43:27,640 --> 00:43:28,920
Where have you been?

440
00:43:29,920 --> 00:43:31,160
Why are you acting like this?

441
00:43:32,600 --> 00:43:34,880
You can't just come
and go whenever you want.

442
00:43:36,640 --> 00:43:37,600
I'm sorry.

443
00:43:49,040 --> 00:43:49,800
I missed you.

444
00:43:51,680 --> 00:43:52,920
I missed you so much, you know?

445
00:43:54,400 --> 00:43:55,440
I missed you too.

446
00:44:30,880 --> 00:44:32,560
The authorities are
watching me all the time.

447
00:44:34,480 --> 00:44:35,800
But I kept my promise.

448
00:44:37,920 --> 00:44:39,720
And we finally got to
see the rainbow together.

449
00:44:41,800 --> 00:44:43,680
I really want to punch you, you know?

450
00:45:29,640 --> 00:45:30,840
You were too busy crying.

451
00:45:31,360 --> 00:45:32,640
The rainbow is already gone.

452
00:45:33,320 --> 00:45:35,280
You're the one who kept crying.

453
00:45:43,640 --> 00:45:45,840
Let's wait for
the next rainbow together.

454
00:46:17,520 --> 00:46:18,960
With such a nice atmosphere,

455
00:46:22,840 --> 00:46:24,160
would you like to dance with me?

456
00:46:25,920 --> 00:46:26,760
No way.

457
00:46:27,120 --> 00:46:28,040
Hey, not yet.

458
00:46:28,240 --> 00:46:28,680
Hmm?

459
00:46:29,720 --> 00:46:31,360
Didn't I already teach you how to dance?

460
00:46:32,960 --> 00:46:34,440
Huh? Don't tell me you forgot.

461
00:46:36,800 --> 00:46:37,640
Do you remember?

462
00:46:38,880 --> 00:46:39,640
You lead.

463
00:46:40,560 --> 00:46:41,160
Ready?

464
00:46:41,560 --> 00:46:43,320
Three, two, one.

465
00:46:49,160 --> 00:46:50,760
You don't remember?

466
00:46:52,280 --> 00:46:53,440
Let's go slowly.

467
00:47:24,080 --> 00:47:27,400
(One year later)

468
00:48:10,600 --> 00:48:11,840
Hey, everyone.

469
00:48:11,840 --> 00:48:13,840
Wow, Captain.

470
00:48:14,120 --> 00:48:14,640
Amazing.

471
00:48:14,640 --> 00:48:15,520
It's me,

472
00:48:15,560 --> 00:48:16,520
- in a whole new form.
- Congratulations.

473
00:48:16,520 --> 00:48:18,000
- Hello.
- Congratulations.

474
00:48:18,000 --> 00:48:19,440
- Thank you, everyone.
- Congratulations, Captain.

475
00:48:19,440 --> 00:48:20,360
Of course.

476
00:48:20,360 --> 00:48:23,120
Everyone, feel free to give me a pat.

477
00:48:23,920 --> 00:48:25,080
This calls for a celebration.

478
00:48:25,080 --> 00:48:26,200
Absolutely.

479
00:48:26,640 --> 00:48:28,240
- Truly amazing.
- That's great.

480
00:48:29,200 --> 00:48:30,640
- Thank you, everyone.
- Sure.

481
00:48:40,920 --> 00:48:41,760
Tangme.

482
00:48:43,080 --> 00:48:43,760
Do you see this?

483
00:48:45,440 --> 00:48:46,680
I did it.

484
00:48:48,080 --> 00:48:48,640
Look.

485
00:48:50,080 --> 00:48:51,920
Today marks exactly the five-year anniversary.

486
00:48:51,920 --> 00:48:54,760
since the mysterious fire
in Nakhon Sawan.

487
00:48:55,320 --> 00:48:57,600
It has become a legend of Pak Nam Pho.

488
00:48:58,160 --> 00:48:59,600
Some people believe

489
00:48:59,680 --> 00:49:01,840
the killer has already died.

490
00:49:02,440 --> 00:49:04,520
Others say he's still alive

491
00:49:04,680 --> 00:49:06,680
and found someone he fell in love with,

492
00:49:07,200 --> 00:49:08,440
who made him stop killing

493
00:49:08,680 --> 00:49:10,640
and disappear to live a secret life.

494
00:49:11,400 --> 00:49:12,880
The motive behind the murders

495
00:49:12,880 --> 00:49:14,200
still remains a mystery.

496
00:49:15,200 --> 00:49:15,880
And today,

497
00:49:15,960 --> 00:49:19,960
we're going to tell you the legend
of the fire murders of Pak Nam Pho.

498
00:49:21,840 --> 00:49:22,840
What's with you?

499
00:49:23,600 --> 00:49:25,040
Why did you suddenly put this news on?

500
00:49:25,680 --> 00:49:26,720
You're asking for trouble.

501
00:49:27,480 --> 00:49:28,600
Let's play some music instead.

502
00:49:35,880 --> 00:49:37,480
I knew you wanted to hear this song.

503
00:49:44,240 --> 00:49:45,560
Listen to this song to the end first,

504
00:49:46,800 --> 00:49:48,120
then you can play whatever you want.

505
00:49:52,480 --> 00:49:53,880
I really miss this road.

506
00:49:55,360 --> 00:49:57,680
It reminds me of when I first came
to Nakhon Sawan for the case.

507
00:49:59,720 --> 00:50:01,240
You're pretty sentimental too.

508
00:50:06,800 --> 00:50:07,800
You were too busy playing music.

509
00:50:08,360 --> 00:50:10,040
The rainbow is almost gone.

510
00:50:10,600 --> 00:50:11,840
Hey, then pull over right here.

511
00:50:12,280 --> 00:50:13,000
Right here?

512
00:50:14,320 --> 00:50:16,760
When are you going to
stop being so impatient?

513
00:50:29,440 --> 00:50:30,280
What do you think

514
00:50:30,960 --> 00:50:32,040
the end of the rainbow

515
00:50:32,320 --> 00:50:33,280
looks like?

516
00:50:37,240 --> 00:50:38,280
If we keep going,

517
00:50:39,040 --> 00:50:41,160
do you think we'll get there before
the rainbow disappears?

518
00:50:43,520 --> 00:50:44,480
I don't think we'll make it.

519
00:50:46,840 --> 00:50:48,240
Even if we don't get there,

520
00:50:50,120 --> 00:50:51,080
that's okay.

521
00:50:53,040 --> 00:50:54,560
Then we'll never settle our argument

522
00:50:55,280 --> 00:50:56,880
about how many colors
a rainbow really has.

523
00:50:57,800 --> 00:51:00,880
I already told you,
a rainbow has six colors.

524
00:51:01,400 --> 00:51:02,680
You can see seven if you want,

525
00:51:03,520 --> 00:51:04,640
but I still see six.

526
00:51:09,080 --> 00:51:09,800
Actually,

527
00:51:11,440 --> 00:51:13,320
I think I've seen
a rainbow up close before.

528
00:51:15,000 --> 00:51:16,000
Really close.

529
00:51:18,200 --> 00:51:18,840
So close

530
00:51:19,520 --> 00:51:20,320
it was right in front of my face.

531
00:51:21,920 --> 00:51:23,920
Did you sneak off to see it by yourself?

532
00:51:30,320 --> 00:51:36,320
♪You are my light,
you're shining so bright♪

533
00:51:36,640 --> 00:51:42,320
♪Here we are in the world all alone♪

534
00:51:43,440 --> 00:51:49,440
♪It's getting late, but I will wait♪

535
00:51:50,280 --> 00:51:54,480
♪I will always wait for you♪

536
00:51:58,440 --> 00:52:01,520
If I could spend eternity with you,

537
00:52:02,800 --> 00:52:05,840
eternity would feel like
the blink of an eye.

538
00:52:07,360 --> 00:52:09,280
But even if it were only
the blink of an eye,

539
00:52:11,800 --> 00:52:15,200
I would cherish every moment
for as long as I could.

540
00:53:01,640 --> 00:53:05,960
♪In a love that can never be real♪

541
00:53:08,520 --> 00:53:13,280
♪You gaze in my soul
and share what I feel♪

542
00:53:15,600 --> 00:53:20,480
♪Gray days all fade
away, I'm healed♪

543
00:53:22,400 --> 00:53:27,160
♪My dull world starts
to glow and shine♪

544
00:53:29,760 --> 00:53:36,680
♪Bound by fate we cannot break,
silent thoughts we both share♪

545
00:53:36,800 --> 00:53:42,560
♪Found a light no dark can shake♪

546
00:53:43,480 --> 00:53:48,800
♪We make a wish toward rainbow's end♪

547
00:53:50,880 --> 00:53:56,040
♪Chase the dream beyond the bend♪

548
00:53:58,000 --> 00:54:04,560
♪Though this hope can
never reach the ground♪

549
00:54:04,640 --> 00:54:09,840
♪You painted hues in my barren land♪

550
00:54:13,600 --> 00:54:20,520
♪In lonely nights I used to fall,
till your eyes broke through my shell♪

551
00:54:20,920 --> 00:54:27,800
♪Hidden love we dare not tell,
sweet moments time can't quell♪

552
00:54:29,680 --> 00:54:36,240
♪Bound by fate we cannot break,
silent thoughts we both share♪

553
00:54:36,840 --> 00:54:42,680
♪Found a light no dark can shake♪

554
00:54:43,600 --> 00:54:49,360
♪We make a wish toward rainbow's end♪

555
00:54:51,240 --> 00:54:56,840
♪Chase the dream beyond the bend♪

556
00:54:58,280 --> 00:55:04,680
♪Though this hope can
never reach the ground♪

557
00:55:04,920 --> 00:55:10,440
♪You painted hues in my barren land♪

558
00:55:40,480 --> 00:55:45,320
♪Wish stays locked inside my heart♪

559
00:55:47,680 --> 00:55:53,120
♪Colored memories never depart♪

560
00:55:55,120 --> 00:56:00,400
♪Love that's doomed yet stole my heart♪

561
00:56:02,640 --> 00:56:08,600
♪Love that's doomed yet stole my heart♪

